=== accelerator-linear --help ===
Usage: accelerator-linear <COMMAND>

Commands:
  create      Create an issue from a work-item file or an explicit title
  update      Update an issue's fields
  show        Show an issue as JSON
  search      Search issues, rendering a JSON envelope
  comment     Comment on an issue
  transition  Transition an issue to a named workflow state
  attach      Attach a link or a file to an issue
  init        Verify credentials, list teams, or discover a team's states
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

=== accelerator-linear create --help ===
Create an issue from a work-item file or an explicit title

Usage: accelerator-linear create [OPTIONS] [FILE]

Arguments:
  [FILE]  A work-item file whose frontmatter and body seed the issue

Options:
      --title <TITLE>          The issue title (the no-file mode)
      --body-file <BODY_FILE>  A Markdown body file for the no-file mode
  -q, --quiet                  
  -h, --help                   Print help

=== accelerator-linear update --help ===
Update an issue's fields

Usage: accelerator-linear update [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>  

Options:
      --title <TITLE>              
      --description <DESCRIPTION>  
      --state <STATE>              
      --assignee-id <ASSIGNEE_ID>  
      --priority <PRIORITY>        
  -q, --quiet                      
  -h, --help                       Print help

=== accelerator-linear show --help ===
Show an issue as JSON

Usage: accelerator-linear show [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>  

Options:
      --comments <COMMENTS>  Include the most recent N comments
  -h, --help                 Print help

=== accelerator-linear search --help ===
Search issues, rendering a JSON envelope

Usage: accelerator-linear search [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --state <STATE>        
      --assignee <ASSIGNEE>  
      --label <LABEL>        
      --text <TEXT>          
      --limit <LIMIT>        
  -q, --quiet                
  -h, --help                 Print help

=== accelerator-linear comment --help ===
Comment on an issue

Usage: accelerator-linear comment <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add   Add a Markdown comment to an issue
  help  Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

=== accelerator-linear transition --help ===
Transition an issue to a named workflow state

Usage: accelerator-linear transition [OPTIONS] <ID> [STATE]

Arguments:
  <ID>     
  [STATE]  The target state name, positional or via `--state`

Options:
      --state <STATE>  
  -q, --quiet          
  -h, --help           Print help

=== accelerator-linear attach --help ===
Attach a link or a file to an issue

Usage: accelerator-linear attach [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>  

Options:
      --url <URL>      
      --file <FILE>    
      --title <TITLE>  
  -q, --quiet          
  -h, --help           Print help

=== accelerator-linear init --help ===
Verify credentials, list teams, or discover a team's states

Usage: accelerator-linear init <COMMAND>

Commands:
  verify      Verify credentials without printing them
  list-teams  List the teams the token can see
  discover    Discover a team's workflow states
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

